    "body": "fix on issue/2121-rapid-at-clearance-in-stock · PR #2138 · pinned by `clearance_in_stock.rs` (8 tests: the Contour repro and a Slot convicted and the post held; the same plane after a Face is clean), `verify::prior_traverse` and `verify::traverse_solids` unit tests · merges when reviewed\n\nWhat was found beyond the repro:\n- Only the mill column law (d) had the clearance gate. The turning (meridian), rotary and radial rapid laws judge every rapid and are unchanged.\n- Removing the gate alone refused two kinds of legal program, so two re-reads were added for the new convictions only: against the program ahead (Face first, then a low plane) and against the solids under the tool (a 3+2 plane over a tilted block: the column is capped at the block's highest corner).\n- A refusal at command creation was built and dropped: it cannot see where the rapids run and refused four standing fixtures. The plane is named at creation instead (MCP `warning`); the app showing it is #2131.\n",
